# REQUIRES: python-api
# What the assembly of the loop over frames assumes of the text that the
# builder emits (#302, docs/python-frames.md, the frames inside one
# activation), on the CPU in double and mixed precision, the scenario `loop`
# of Inputs/python_frames.py. In the module of an evaluator (the whole
# potential, the dependent terms, a program with a barostat, a triclinic
# cell) the loop over frames holds no allocation of the stack in any
# spelling, no call in the generic form, and no argument of the entry that a
# frame replaces, and the rows stand before it. The stack of the entry is
# as deep at the boundary after frame 201 as after frame 1, to the byte
# (the entry never returns: memory of the stack taken in the loop, by the
# builder or by a pass, is a depth that grows); and the bytes in use of the
# allocator, read as python-memory.test reads them, grow by less than 4096
# from frame 101 to frame 201, in calls of 25 frames (41 bytes a frame pass).
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frames.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide loop CPU Double | FileCheck %s -DMODE="CPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frames.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide loop CPU Mixed | FileCheck %s -DMODE="CPU Mixed"
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the loop over frames of the whole potential: {{.*}}; in it 0 allocations of the stack, 0 calls in the generic form, 0 arguments of the entry that a frame replaces; {{[0-9]+}} allocations of the stack before it: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the loop over frames of the dependent terms: {{.*}}; in it 0 allocations of the stack, 0 calls in the generic form, 0 arguments of the entry that a frame replaces; {{[0-9]+}} allocations of the stack before it: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the loop over frames of a program with a barostat: {{.*}}; in it 0 allocations of the stack, 0 calls in the generic form, 0 arguments of the entry that a frame replaces; {{[0-9]+}} allocations of the stack before it: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the loop over frames of a triclinic cell: {{.*}}; in it 0 allocations of the stack, 0 calls in the generic form, 0 arguments of the entry that a frame replaces; {{[0-9]+}} allocations of the stack before it: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the stack of the entry of the whole potential at the boundary after frames 1, 101, and 201: {{[0-9]+}} bytes, then +0 and +0 bytes (bound 0): True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the bytes in use of the allocator with the whole potential from frame 101 to frame 201: {{.*}} (bound 4096): True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the stack of the entry of the dependent terms at the boundary after frames 1, 101, and 201: {{[0-9]+}} bytes, then +0 and +0 bytes (bound 0): True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the bytes in use of the allocator with the dependent terms from frame 101 to frame 201: {{.*}} (bound 4096): True
# CHECK: loop passed
